      "sourceHash": "9df3a27315fd178c99d0b40f48881704af2db3ced8edd42c2ecde1e04009f339",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "So we built a custom attribute Directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 7.29,
          "en": "Next, I wanna build a custom structural Directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.29,
          "end": 10.56,
          "en": "and I wanna build a custom structural Directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.56,
          "end": 15.51,
          "en": "that makes rendering content based on user status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 18.27,
          "en": "even easier than with this if statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.27,
          "end": 21.39,
          "en": "or the ngIf Directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.39,
          "end": 23.88,
          "en": "For that, I'll create a new Directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 26.433,
          "en": "and I will now do that with help of the CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.57,
          "end": 31.953,
          "en": "and name this Directive auth Directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.27,
          "end": 35.94,
          "en": "And it should be generated in the auth folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.94,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "which is why I will add this auth folder prefix in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 43.803,
          "en": "of the name so that it's added in this folder here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "I will also add --skip-tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 52.683,
          "en": "so that the extra testing file isn't generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 58.443,
          "en": "and yep, that should be ng g d.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "So with that, we have this auth Directive TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 68.7,
          "en": "and as you see, that gives us a class with that decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 68.7,
          "end": 72.66,
          "en": "which has this selector here, which is quite convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 72.66,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "Now what do we want to do in this Directive?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 79.44,
          "en": "How do we want to use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 79.44,
          "end": 83.49,
          "en": "Well, in the end, the idea is that we can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 83.49,
          "end": 87.003,
          "en": "on some element that should be rendered conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "So for example, here on this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 96,
          "en": "and I wanna be able to add my appAuth Directive here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 96,
          "end": 98.49000000000001,
          "en": "and then set the type of user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 98.49000000000001,
          "end": 100.92,
          "en": "for which this element should be shown on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 100.92,
          "end": 104.75999999999999,
          "en": "for example, admin or guest or user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 104.75999999999999,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "These are the three types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "of users this application supports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 110.733,
          "en": "So in this case, it would be admin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 116.72999999999999,
          "en": "That's kind of how I want to be able to use this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 119.1,
          "en": "though since it'll be a structural Directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 119.1,
          "end": 120.93,
          "en": "we'll need to add an asterisk here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 122.53,
          "en": "but I'll get back to this later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.26,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "Therefore, back in this auth Directive TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 132.12,
          "en": "we will definitely need to accept an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.12,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "because we need that user for which we want to show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "the element on which this Directive is added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "We need that user type as an input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 145.65,
          "en": "So I'll add a property called userType",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.65,
          "end": 148.35,
          "en": "and set up an input with help of the input function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 150.87,
          "en": "though again, you could of course also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 150.87,
          "end": 152.28300000000002,
          "en": "the input decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.18,
          "end": 156.39,
          "en": "Here, I'll set this to be a required input, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.39,
          "end": 159,
          "en": "because this Directive needs to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 161.79,
          "en": "for which user the content should be shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "This is some required information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "And the kind of value I want to get through",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 171.03300000000002,
          "en": "that input should be of type Permission,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 175.32,
          "en": "which is a type I set up in my auth.model file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.32,
          "end": 178.68,
          "en": "which is in the end, this union type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.68,
          "end": 182.37,
          "en": "which combines three string literal values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.37,
          "end": 185.703,
          "en": "for the allowed values that I want to take here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 189.33,
          "en": "So that's the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 192.72,
          "en": "The next important building block is that we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.72,
          "end": 197.523,
          "en": "to find out which kind of user is currently locked in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.39,
          "end": 200.13,
          "en": "and that's some information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.13,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "that's managed by the auth service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 204.72,
          "en": "There, whenever the user authenticate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.72,
          "end": 208.233,
          "en": "we update this activePermission Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.57999999999998,
          "end": 210.9,
          "en": "Now, I mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.9,
          "end": 214.17000000000002,
          "en": "that you can inject services into Directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.17000000000002,
          "end": 216.18,
          "en": "and that is therefore what I'll do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.18,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "I'll inject the authService with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 223.59,
          "en": "of the inject function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 223.59,
          "end": 227.28300000000002,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could use the constructor as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.24,
          "end": 231.42000000000002,
          "en": "and we can then use this service to find out which kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.42000000000002,
          "end": 234.03,
          "en": "of user is currently locked in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.03,
          "end": 238.82999999999998,
          "en": "But what do we do with that information now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.82999999999998,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "Well, now here in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 244.74,
          "en": "we can use the Effect function, which is provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 244.74,
          "end": 248.37,
          "en": "about which you also learned earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.37,
          "end": 253.37,
          "en": "to run some code whenever some Signal value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 257.01,
          "en": "And here, I wanna run some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.01,
          "end": 260.7,
          "en": "whenever the user permission changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 260.7,
          "end": 264.003,
          "en": "or whenever this input value here changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 265.11,
          "end": 270.11,
          "en": "So we pass a function to this Effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 271.2,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "This will be the code that should be executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 275.55,
          "en": "and in there, I wanna check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 275.55,
          "end": 279.6,
          "en": "if this authService.activePermission,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 279.6,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "if I read that Signal value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 286.623,
          "en": "I wanna check if that is equal to this.userType,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 287.49,
          "end": 290.58299999999997,
          "en": "so to this input Signal value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 292.23,
          "end": 294.81,
          "en": "If that is equal, I know that the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 294.81,
          "end": 297.45,
          "en": "on which this Directive is added should be shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 297.45,
          "end": 300.843,
          "en": "So for now, I'll just console.log SHOW ELEMENT,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 302.85,
          "end": 305.7,
          "en": "else it should be removed from the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 305.7,
          "end": 309.66,
          "en": "because else we have a user that's not of the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 309.66,
          "end": 312,
          "en": "of user for which this element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 312,
          "end": 314.673,
          "en": "on which this Directive is added should be shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 315.51,
          "end": 319.413,
          "en": "So here, I'll log DO NOT SHOW ELEMENT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 322.41,
          "end": 324.24,
          "en": "And since we're using Effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 324.24,
          "end": 327.96,
          "en": "Angular will set up subscriptions for activePermission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 327.96,
          "end": 331.59,
          "en": "and userType, and re-execute that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 331.59,
          "end": 335.14,
          "en": "whenever either of these two Signal values changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 338.73,
          "en": "so that this code will run again and again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 338.73,
          "end": 342.003,
          "en": "as the active user's permission status changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 342.99,
          "end": 345.03,
          "en": "So if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 345.03,
          "end": 349.11,
          "en": "and you go back to the app.component.html file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 349.11,
          "end": 352.743,
          "en": "you can add appAuth, this Directive here, to this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 357.69,
          "en": "but then there, we actually need to set a different kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 357.69,
          "end": 360.93,
          "en": "of input because here I named it userType,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 360.93,
          "end": 364.5,
          "en": "but we can use the same trick as before and assign an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 364.5,
          "end": 368.64,
          "en": "so that we can use the Directive selector attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 368.64,
          "end": 372.423,
          "en": "as a directly bindable input for this Directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 373.44,
          "end": 377.163,
          "en": "whilst internally using a more descriptive property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 379.02,
          "end": 382.17,
          "en": "With that, we can bind the appAuth property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 382.17,
          "end": 385.14,
          "en": "on this paragraph where we add this Directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 385.14,
          "end": 389.07,
          "en": "and we can set it to a hard-coded string like admin here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 389.07,
          "end": 392.49,
          "en": "so that this element should only be shown for admins,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 392.49,
          "end": 394.71,
          "en": "though at the moment, it will always be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 394.71,
          "end": 396.54,
          "en": "because at the moment, we're just logging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 396.54,
          "end": 397.89300000000003,
          "en": "something to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 399.15,
          "end": 402,
          "en": "But with all that, if we save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 402,
          "end": 406.92,
          "en": "we don't see anything here, nothing new at least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 406.92,
          "end": 408.99,
          "en": "and we don't get any new output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 408.99,
          "end": 412.74,
          "en": "because whilst we did create this Directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 412.74,
          "end": 414.93,
          "en": "Angular isn't aware of it yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 414.93,
          "end": 418.89300000000003,
          "en": "You need to register it since it's a Standalone Directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 419.82,
          "end": 422.52,
          "en": "So in the Component where you want to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 422.52,
          "end": 424.41,
          "en": "in this case the AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 424.41,
          "end": 427.14,
          "en": "you need to add it to the imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 427.14,
          "end": 430.62,
          "en": "So here, we need to add the AuthDirective,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 431.79,
          "end": 433.863,
          "en": "and also add this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 436.95,
          "end": 438.495,
          "en": "With that if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 438.495,
          "end": 441.03,
          "en": "you now see DO NOT SHOW ELEMENT here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 441.03,
          "end": 444.873,
          "en": "because initially, the user is not logged in as an admin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 446.58,
          "end": 450.87,
          "en": "But if I now, for example, enter admin@example.com admin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 452.04,
          "end": 455.343,
          "en": "and click log in, you see SHOW ELEMENT gets logged.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 456.27,
          "end": 458.55,
          "en": "So this Directive seems to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 458.55,
          "end": 462.12,
          "en": "but of course, it's not yet changing the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
